6. Conclusion

Kruskal’s algorithm provides an efficient method for designing a minimum-cost communication network for hospital departments. In this project, the hospital departments are represented as vertices, and the possible communication cables are represented as weighted edges.
The algorithm sorts all communication cables according to their installation costs and selects the minimum-cost edges without forming any cycle. By applying this method, all five hospital departments are connected using four communication cables.
The program calculates the minimum total installation cost as Rs. 85. This demonstrates that Kruskal’s algorithm can help reduce network installation expenses while ensuring that every department is connected to the network.
The project also improves our understanding of graph representation, greedy algorithms, sorting techniques, cycle detection, and Minimum Spanning Trees using C++.
